# Keep line endings stable across Windows and Linux.
#
# Without this, a Windows tool rewriting a data file with CRLF produces a diff
# in which EVERY line has changed, even though no content has. That happened to
# four files here: `longtail_sample_2026-07-25.txt` showed 10,000 changed lines
# for zero content changes.
#
# Two harms, and the second is the serious one:
#   1. Review becomes impossible -- a real one-line change is invisible in a
#      10,000-line diff.
#   2. GitHub push protection scans the diff, so a full-file rewrite re-exposes
#      every line to secret scanning. This dataset legitimately contains
#      repository *names* shaped like credentials (see security/), and a
#      spurious full-file diff drags them back through that check for no reason.
*.jsonl  text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.ps1    text eol=crlf
*.png    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.docx   binary
